# SPARKLE PUBLIC KEY (ed25519)
# ============================================
# THIS FILE IS A PLACEHOLDER STUB. The real public key is set per
# deployment by running:
#
#     ./Scripts/sign-sparkle-update.sh keygen
#
# After keygen prints the new public key, replace the body of this
# file with the public key in PEM format, for example:
#
#     -----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----
#     <44-character base64 string ending in '='>
#     -----END PUBLIC KEY-----
#
# THEN update the same base64 string in TWO places:
#
#   1. THIS FILE (Resources/sparkle-pubkey.pem)   — record / reference
#   2. Riptide.entitlements  ->  <key>SUPublicEDKey</key><string>...</string>
#
# Sparkle.framework reads SUPublicEDKey from the app bundle's entitlements
# at runtime, so (2) is what the running app actually uses. (1) is purely
# a checked-in record so future maintainers know which public key corresponds
# to which private key generation.
#
# SECURITY:
#   - This file MAY be committed (the public key is, by definition, public).
#   - The corresponding PRIVATE key lives at:
#         ~/Keys/riptide-sparkle-ed25519.pem   (mode 0600)
#     and in the SPARKLE_PRIVATE_KEY GitHub Secret for CI. NEVER commit it.
#   - If this file is ever replaced, also rotate SPARKLE_PRIVATE_KEY in
#     GitHub Secrets, otherwise the old key will still be trusted by CI.
#
# CURRENT VALUE: PLACEHOLDER — replace before first release.
# ============================================
PLACEHOLDER_PUBLIC_KEY_REPLACE_ME
